\description{
\strong{Get the standings as of a round: basic (W-L, points, home / away / last-10
records), calendar (per-round result streaks), streaks (longest win / loss
runs) or aheadbehind (records when ahead / behind / tied after Q1, the half
and Q3), one row per team.}

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://api-live.euroleague.net/v3/competitions/\{competition_code\}/seasons/\{season_code\}/rounds/\{round\}/\{kind\}}

The standings live under a \strong{round}, not the season: pass the \code{round}
number the table should be as of (the \code{round} column of
\code{\link[=euroleague_rounds]{euroleague_rounds()}}). The season winner block of the payload is dropped
(it is \code{null} while the season is in progress).
}
\details{
Unofficial, keyless API, not supported by Euroleague Basketball; hoopR only
wraps it (wrap-only: payloads are not redistributed as release assets). This
function mirrors its sdv-py twin of the same name: same arguments, defaults
and snake_case columns, one row per sdv-py row.

A failed request raises a classed condition instead of returning an empty
frame, mirroring sdv-py's error vocabulary: a 404 is \code{hoopR_no_data}, a
400 / 422 is \code{hoopR_invalid_request}, any other failure (another status, a
transport error, a non-JSON body) is \code{hoopR_fetch_error}; all three inherit
\code{hoopR_error}.
}
